      "title": "Massive student-led rally marches in Belgrade ahead of Serbian election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/serbia-election-student-list-rally-belgrade-aleksandar-vucic",
      "description": "<p>Student List movement hopes to oust the party of veteran leader Aleksandar Vucic in a pivotal vote on Sunday</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/22/serbia-election-student-protests-explainer-key-issues\">Explained: what’s at stake in Serbia’s election? The key players, main issues and potential fallout</a></p></li></ul><p>About 150,000 supporters of Serbia’s opposition student movement rallied in central Belgrade on Thursday, seeking to oust the party of veteran leader Aleksandar Vucic in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/22/serbia-election-student-protests-explainer-key-issues\">crunch parliamentary elections</a> this weekend.</p><p>The Student List, a leaderless movement of student-backed candidates, wants to end more than 14 years of rule by Vucic’s rightwing populist Serbian Progressive party (SNS) in Sunday’s vote.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/serbia-election-student-list-rally-belgrade-aleksandar-vucic\">Continue reading...</a>",
